dInterfaceCallSite` (port of\n25|  `reviewer_callsite_test.go`, extended to pre- AND post-hold plants) passes,\n26|  i.e. the child witness renames real files through the production entry while\n27|  the child census refuses both unlisted sites. Census gate passes on the clean\n28|  tree.\n29|- Five own plants in `replaceDurably`, each gate exit 1 with a violation at the\n30|  planted site: (p1) second `Rename` at a later unlisted position — refused;\n31|  (p2) method value `rn := filesystem.Rename` invoked pre-hold — refused with\n32|  explicit \"method value/site escapes\"; (p3) call inside a deferred func —\n33|  refused; (p4) edge in an `if false` branch — refused (no constant folding);\n34|  (p5) `goto` bypass shifting lines — refused by site identity.\n35|- p6 (line-preserving `goto` over the guard to an inventoried site): census\n36|  exit 0, zero violations — ADMITTED by the static census, which enforces\n37|  lexical guard-precedes-call, not CFG dominance. Behaviorally inert: all four\n38|  HOLD writers carry the guard as the lexically-first statement, so no\n39|  intra-function path can reach any call without executing it; a zero-hold\n40|  witness through the p6 bypass is still refused (`require exclusive hold`).\n41|  Recorded as a P3 hardening observation (CFG-aware dominance or goto/label\n42|  scan), not verdict-blocking: the census document claims lexical precedence\n43|  and the implementation matches the claim.\n44|- Former method-spelling admission predicate is removed; remaining `Name() ==`\n45|  uses are hold-guard recognition (`requireHold*`) and the `CreateExclusive`\n46|  backend definition — fail-closed detectors, matching the narrowed census\n47|  claim. The 119-site/90-group inventory carries per-group production\n48|  justifications. Narrowing mutant `writepath-interface-callsite-skip`\n49|  (preserves method identity, drops site/hold admission) killed by the\n50|  regression, 2/2 runs. Rogues suite 28/28 pass.\n51|\n52|## F2 (CR11 P2) — repaired and verified\n53|\n54|`ensureConfigBindingLocked` validates the store-side association (:246-254)\n55|before publishing the target sidecar (:256-280); the store index is derived\n56|after authority (:285-293). Committed trio green:\n57|`TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`,\n58|`TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`,\n59|`TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen`, plus the CR11\n60|`TestConfigBindingSurvivesReopenAndRejectsForeignRoot` control.\n61|Own probes (scratch, exact final source): target-side crash injection (fails\n62|the authoritative rename, unlike the producer's index injection) leaves both\n63|records absent and a retry converges; reverse-ordering consequence\n64|(index present, sidecar deleted) is refused already at `Open` with resource\n65|mismatch and the stranded index stays intact, never silently rebound; a second\n66|store refused against a target bound elsewhere leaves both associations\n67|untouched. All pass.\n68|\n69|## Mutation batteries (exact final source, fixed harness)\n70|\n71|Methodology note: `go -overlay` silently ignores mappings whose keys are\n72|symlink-resolved (`/private/tmp/...`) while the build resolves the logical\n73|(`/tmp/...`) path. My first `/tmp` runs therefore reported false survivors;\n74|rerunning from a symlink-free copy reproduces the producer's kills, and direct\n75|source application confirms the mechanism. Producer's 47-killed evidence is\n76|consistent with a non-symlinked run location and stands.\n77|\n78|- Config (`mutations_v4.py`, 14 probes): neutral passed + 13 narrowing mutants\n79|  killed by the expected named tests, 0 survivors.\n80|- Host Trust (`mutations.py`, 35 probes): neutral passed + 34 narrowing\n81|  mutants killed by the expected named tests, 0 survivors — including\n82|  `hold-state-root-skip` (killed by\n83|  `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsForeignConfigStateRoot`) and the preserve-token\n84|  `compensate-verify-before-restore` order swap (behavioral-suite kill).\n85|- Three reviewer-owned narrowing mutants on unmutated arms, each killed twice\n86|  by the expected test: `reviewer-trust-version-downgrade` (admits exactly\n87|  `0.9.0`; `TestDecodeTrustRefusals/downgraded_version`),\n88|  `reviewer-credential-format-leak` (emits exactly the credential ID;\n89|  `TestTrustRedaction`), `reviewer-exclusion-prerollback-skip` (admits exactly\n90|  pre-rollback copies; `TestExcludedConfigDirName/pre-rollback_copy`).\n91|- Key mutants rerun twice for determinism (callsite-skip, hold-state-root-skip,\n92|  compensate-verify-before-restore, all three own): 2/2 kills.\n93|\n94|## Suites, hygiene, bounds\n95|\n96|- `go test ./... -count=1`: exit 0, all packages ok. `-race` on\n97|  `internal/config` and `internal/hosttrust`: exit 0. `go vet ./...` (native\n98|  and `GOOS=windows`): exit 0. `gofmt -l`: clean. `go mod tidy -diff`: exit 0\n99|  (offline). Builds: native, darwin/arm64, linux/arm64, windows/amd64 exit 0.\n100|  Coverage: config 92.9%, hosttrust 76.4%, peeridentity 97.5%, localstore\n101|  83.8%, secprim 94.4%. Validation log: 26/26 green.\n102|- Changed paths: 74 (17 tracked + 57 untracked), restricted to\n103|  `internal/` source/test/harness, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`, `go.mod/go.sum`.\n104|  No `__pycache__`/`.pyc`, no `task-board.config.json`, no stray plant files.\n105|  README tool row describes the all-indirect-call policy and exact exceptions.\n106|  `golang.org/x/tools` is test-only (census). Literal RPC-manifest overlap is\n107|  `README.md` only; no RPC implementation path absorbed. `go.mod` adds only\n108|  `x/tools` (+2 indirect).\n109|- AC accounting: **19 of 21 rows driven**; rows 15 (Windows ACL runtime) and\n110|  21 (downstream replication consumers) remain stated bounds, not passes. No\n111|  post-lock-release dispatch, mesh-wide revocation, physical power-loss, or\n112|  human-verification guarantee inferred. RPC transport/admission outside leaf.\n113|\n114|## Verdict routing\n115|\n116|Accept. F1/F2 counterexamples are repaired with committed regressions,\n117|narrowing mutants, and independent probes; hygiene is clean; evidence is\n118|attached as `TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev12.md` (this file) and\n119|`TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev12.tar.gz`. No product edits, no\n120|`commit_ack`, no integration by this reviewer.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
